course: dictionary
lesson: 8444
title: Safety: more than being safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Safety means being protected from danger, harm or injury. It also means the care and rules that stop accidents, like road safety or fire safety. «They swam to safety» means they reached a safe place.
explain: «The most important words you can say are your address, which is why learning it by heart is a real safety skill.» Here a safety skill is something you learn to keep yourself protected. The clue is "learning it by heart": you need it to get help if you are in trouble.
explain: Safety is a word that can mean different things, so check the words around it. Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. "For your safety" can become "to keep you protected", and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Safety means being protected from danger, harm or injury.
fact: Road safety means you stop, look and listen before you cross.
fact: «Safety first» is a phrase that means keeping people protected is the most important thing.
fact: «Safety» can also mean a safe place, as in «They swam to safety».
fact: In American football, a safety is a way of scoring 2 points, so the word can have a special meaning in a sport.
exercise: «They swam to safety.» What does safety mean here? | A kind of boat | A swimming race | A loud shout | *A safe place
exercise: Which of these is a piece of safety gear? | Spoon | Umbrella | *Helmet | Pencil case
exercise: A teacher says, «Safety first on the school trip.» What does she mean? | Running ahead of the group | Eating lunch as quickly as you can | *Keeping everyone protected comes first | Ignoring the rules to have more fun
test: «The most important words you can say are your address, which is why learning it by heart is a real safety skill.» What is a safety skill? | *Something that helps keep you protected | A word for a map | A way to win a game | A kind of pencil
test: Which is the best example of road safety? | Running across the road to catch the bus | *Stop, look and listen before you cross | Crossing with your eyes shut | Playing ball in the street
exam: In «Stunt performers are trained professionals who rehearse with safety teams and hidden safety gear», what does safety gear mean? | Clothes for a party | Tools for cooking | Toys for the playground | *Equipment that protects people from harm
